        "original_id": "ac9acd7b-2e79-52f6-b642-d055b9a27ca9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Big Sean, Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, Mike Posner, Kelly Rowland, Lil Wayne, Rick Ross, DJ Khaled\n- Groups: B2K, The Olympicks, Triple C's\n- Projects: Detroit, I Am Not a Human Being, Teflon Don, Custom Cars & Cycles, Kiss The Ring, Lay It on Me\n- Places: Detroit, Michigan\n- Topics: music careers, hip-hop production, featured vocals\n\nFacts:\n- Jhené Aiko began her music career by contributing vocals and appearing in several music videos for the R&B group B2K.\n- The Olympicks originated in Detroit, Michigan.\n- The Olympicks worked on hip-hop projects including Lil Wayne's I Am Not a Human Being, Rick Ross' Teflon Don, Triple C's Custom Cars & Cycles, and DJ Khaled's Kiss The Ring.\n- Big Sean's mixtape Detroit includes the American singers Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, and Mike Posner.\n- The Olympicks were involved in the production of Big Sean's mixtape Detroit.\n- Lay It on Me is a song by Kelly Rowland featuring two rap verses from Big Sean.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
